{"result":"{
  "id": "19426",
  "key": "SFCC-863",
  "summary": "Suppress placeholder DntNotification modal; route consent through Didomi",
  "description": "\\*\\*Context\\*\\*\nSurfaced while investigating SFCC-860's Lighthouse `categories.performance` finding (LCP 6.4s / score 0.1) against a real deployed build. The Largest Contentful Paint element turned out not to be an image — the homepage currently has none — but literal placeholder text inside a modal:\n> \"Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua...\"\nTraced to `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/hooks/use-dnt-notification.js`'s `DntNotification` component, rendered unconditionally in the \\*\\*base\\*\\* `_app/index.jsx` ({{}}) — Zimmermann has no override for `_app` yet, so this base behaviour is live as-is on every tier. Salesforce's own source comment confirms it's not meant to ship: `// Placeholder for the consent tracking form for demonstration purposes`.\nIt auto-opens via a `useEffect` whenever `selectedDnt === undefined` (i.e. on every fresh session with no stored preference — `selectedDnt` comes from `useDNT()`'s `auth.getDnt()`, reading the real SLAS/DNT cookie, so there is no config-level default that suppresses the auto-open; confirmed no `getConfig()?.app?.dntNotificationEnabled`-style toggle exists, unlike e.g. `storeLocatorEnabled`). That's exactly why a fresh, cookie-less Lighthouse run measures it as the LCP element — it's the first substantial content to appear.\n\\*\\*Why this matters beyond performance\\*\\*\nPer `AGENTS.md`'s Consent & Marketing section, Didomi is meant to own all consent gating for this project (`.docs/memory/projectState.md` lists Didomi integration as not-yet-started, REG-054). This base component is not that — it's Salesforce's own demo scaffolding, and real shoppers on any tier without an `_app` override are currently seeing literal \"Lorem ipsum\" copy in a tracking-consent dialog. This is a live UX/compliance bug, not just a Lighthouse number.\n\\*\\*Scope\\*\\*\n- Override `overrides/app/components/_app/index.tsx` (Tier 2 — Global Shell, \"Both Squads — coordinate before touching\" per `protectedFiles.md`; copy-first from `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/components/_app/index.jsx` per `AGENTS.md`'s Copy-first rule) to stop rendering `<DntNotification>`\n- `Header` and `Footer` are both already overridden (`overrides/app/components/header/`, `overrides/app/components/footer/`) — the new `_app` override must import them via relative paths (`../header`, `../footer`), not the base SFCC path, per `.claude/rules/overrideStyling.md`'s \"Importing an already-overridden component from a new component\" section, or Storybook/Vitest will silently exercise the unstyled base versions\n- Decide how this interacts with the broader Didomi integration (REG-054) — does DNT tracking-consent get replaced by a Didomi-driven flow entirely, or does this story just remove the placeholder and Didomi work supersedes it later?\n- Full TypeScript port of `_app` is non-trivial: ~500 lines, many hooks (`useAuthModal`, `useStoreLocatorModal`, `useMultiSite`, `useUpdateShopperContext`, `PageDesignerProvider`, `CurrencyProvider`, checkout header/footer variants, etc.) — budget real review time, not a quick patch\n\\*\\*Acceptance criteria\\*\\*\n- No placeholder/demo consent copy is ever shown to a real shopper on any tier\n- Lighthouse's LCP on the homepage reflects real content, not this modal\n- Header/Footer overrides continue to render correctly through the new `_app` override (spot-check Storybook and the real app, not just tsc)",
  "status": {
    "name": "Code Review",
    "category": "In Progress",
    "color": "yellow"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Story"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "Medium"
  },
  "assignee": {
    "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
    "name": "Tim Lavelle",
    "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
  },
