{"result":"{
  "id": "19421",
  "key": "SFCC-860",
  "summary": "Lighthouse performance score + bundle hygiene (unused JS, preconnect, source maps)",
  "description": "\\*\\*Context\\*\\*\nSurfaced by the SIT Gate's Lighthouse CI job (`lighthouserc.js`, `lighthouse:recommended` preset), running for the first time against a real deployed build (SIT bootstrap, 2026-09-01). Full preset kept as-is rather than narrowed, so these stay visible on every release branch's SIT Gate until fixed.\n\\*\\*Failing assertions\\*\\*\n- `categories.performance` — expected >=0.8, found 0.29 / 0.41 / 0.41 across the 3 LHCI runs. Well below target — this project's own AGENTS.md sets an LCP budget of ≤2s at p75 mobile, so this is a real gap against a stated priority, not just a CI number.\n- `unused-javascript` — expected <=0 flagged instances, found 2\n- `uses-rel-preconnect` — expected <=0, found 1 missing preconnect origin\n- `valid-source-maps` — expected >=0.9, found 0 (missing source maps for large first-party JS — likely a production build config gap, not a code issue)\n\\*\\*Scope\\*\\*\n- Investigate the low performance score (likely unoptimized bundle / no code-splitting yet at this stage — see AGENTS.md's \"Code splitting: prefer dynamic import() for heavy components not needed on initial render\")\n- Reduce unused JavaScript flagged by the audit\n- Add missing `<link rel=\"preconnect\">` for the flagged origin\n- Restore source map generation/upload for production builds so `valid-source-maps` passes\n\\*\\*Out of scope\\*\\* (separate stories)\n- `csp-xss` — see SFCC-856\n- PWA installability (`installable-manifest`, `service-worker`, `maskable-icon`, `splash-screen`) — see SFCC-855\n- `errors-in-console`, `inspector-issues` (best-practices category) — see companion story\n\\*\\*Status:\\*\\* logged as a known, accepted SIT Gate failure for now, not fixed same-day.",
  "status": {
    "name": "Release Ready",
    "category": "Done",
    "color": "green"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Story"
  },
  "priority": {
